Package: zusvg
Title: Render 'SVG' Images Without System Dependencies
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Samuel", "Ugochukwu", role = "cph",
           comment = "plutosvg and plutovg, bundled in src/vendor"),
    person("The FreeType Project", role = "cph",
           comment = "rasteriser and stroker in src/vendor/plutovg/source/plutovg-ft-*"),
    person("Sean", "Barrett", role = "cph",
           comment = "stb_image, stb_image_write and stb_truetype in src/vendor/plutovg")
  )
Description: Renders 'SVG' documents to native rasters, 'RGBA' arrays and
    'PNG' or 'JPEG' files with bundled copies of the 'plutosvg' and
    'plutovg' C libraries, so it installs from source with no system
    library and draws the same pixels on every platform. Aimed at icons and
    logos: text, filters, masks, patterns, markers and 'CSS' style sheets
    are not rendered.
